{
  "_about": "The owner's overlay transition pack (Mr.YTR _MLT1-18, 2026-10-01): full-frame clips on black, laid over a hard cut with a SCREEN blend, each with its own sound, levelled against the narration. peakFrame = the clip's frame that lands ON the cut (the first frame of the new shot; it and the frame before it are the most covered); peak = peakFrame / fps seconds; audioPeak = seconds into the clip of its loudest 20 ms; coverage = how evenly the two cut frames are covered (0-1); character: flash | burn | leak | film | glitch | streak. Loudness: lufs = the clip sound's loudest 400 ms (BS.1770 momentary loudness, K-weighted, measured on a 10 ms hop with the clip padded by silence: the same measure as public/sfx/sfx_meta.json \"lufs\"), peakDb = its sample peak (dBFS). The planner (src/timeline.py pack_gain) and the renderer (PackTransition.tsx packGain) set each clip's gain from lufs so its loudest moment sits 6 dB under the narration's measured loudness (doc.meta.voiceLufs), a glitch clip 9 dB under, never above 1 (as recorded).",
